  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "refactor",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "Architecture identifiers and config/model associations were duplicated between the central registry and individual configuration constructors.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_3ba7866e756041489a361480d6fa41ed"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The change makes each configuration class declare arch_string and each model class declare config_class. The registry derives its existing three-field records from those attributes, retaining an explicit list of supported models.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_3ba7866e756041489a361480d6fa41ed"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "This reduces repeated registration metadata without introducing automatic discovery. The tradeoff is that registration now depends on correct class attributes rather than independently written registry entries.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_3ba7866e756041489a361480d6fa41ed"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "A standard-library comparison of the parent registry with a symbolic transcription of the new definitions found the same eight architecture/config/model associations.",
        "basis": "execution",
        "evidence": [
          "call_32dbb877939a4f71ac7578d9c4b3c36a"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The normal Config.from_directory interface remains unchanged. Direct subclasses of Config must adapt to the removed expect_arch positional parameter; constructor arch_string keyword overrides no longer determine architecture validation.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_ffd8f68f39794e96a22fbae7c6d4b0e8",
          "call_3ba7866e756041489a361480d6fa41ed",
          "call_f8d7863f37414d09b1b8b7589c31b4e6"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "PR #4, \u201cchore: update config.py,\u201d proposes only \u201ccontaing -> containing.\u201d Its relationship to this change is inferred solely from the shared filename; the task does not make that correction.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_c2666d88a56648eb851c0449f6c8bf8c",
          "call_ffd8f68f39794e96a22fbae7c6d4b0e8",
          "call_3ba7866e756041489a361480d6fa41ed"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #7, \u201cquantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate,\u201d includes config.py's RopeSettings import in its traceback and reports a compiler/environment workaround. The inferred overlap is that unchanged import line, not the architecture-validation logic.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_db2a95295c4049d6af9131a5af11c78b",
          "call_ffd8f68f39794e96a22fbae7c6d4b0e8",
          "call_3ba7866e756041489a361480d6fa41ed"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #15, \u201c`cogito-v1-preview-qwen-32B` generates incoherent output for bpw <= 2.5,\u201d concerns quantization regularization. Issue #21, \u201cBuild Failure on Windows: CUDA 12.4 / PyTorch 2.7.0+cu126 / VS 2022,\u201d concerns native compilation. Neither discussion establishes a connection to this metadata refactor.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_229231c0877f4b7992ed38af8bb50b26",
          "call_37baa277d73b4da08d0b3b17eafe1206",
          "call_3ba7866e756041489a361480d6fa41ed"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "No package import, model loading, inference or GPU test was executed. The registry comparison and assertion check are symbolic/scalar transcriptions, not execution of the changed repository.",
      "Model configuration checks establish architecture-string matching only, not weight-format compatibility or successful model construction. Dimensions, numerical defaults and model-specific execution behavior were not validated.",
      "Literal parent-tree searches do not establish compatibility for external subclasses, dynamic callers or imports of the former gemma module."
    ],
    "links": [],
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Class-owned architecture metadata",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "ARCHITECTURES keeps the keys LlamaForCausalLM, MistralForCausalLM, Qwen2ForCausalLM, Phi3ForCausalLM, Gemma2ForCausalLM, DeciLMForCausalLM, Glm4ForCausalLM and CohereForCausalLM. Each record still exposes architecture, config_class and model_class; the comprehension now obtains all three through the listed model class.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_3ba7866e756041489a361480d6fa41ed"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Config.from_directory reads config.json, requires one supported architectures entry, looks up its config_class and invokes that class with directory and kwargs. Config.__init__ then reads the file again and compares its architecture with self.arch_string instead of a constructor argument. Registry selection and validation therefore share the configuration class's declaration.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_ffd8f68f39794e96a22fbae7c6d4b0e8",
              "call_3ba7866e756041489a361480d6fa41ed"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "MistralConfig and Qwen2Config still inherit LlamaConfig. Their class-level arch_string overrides replace the explicit keyword forwarded through the Llama constructor. The inherited constructor continues passing LlamaModel as the instance's model_class; adding model-class config_class attributes does not change that existing data flow.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_0262c21d7c7641399c7400951435af63",
              "call_3ba7866e756041489a361480d6fa41ed"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "gemma.py is renamed gemma2.py and the registry import follows the rename. The parent-tree literal search for .gemma found only that registry import. The diff provides no compatibility module at the old path.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_5891990f531c4b4492cad94d7305ab83",
              "call_3ba7866e756041489a361480d6fa41ed"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The inspected configs for TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0, mistralai/Mistral-7B-v0.1, Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B, microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct and unsloth/gemma-2-2b respectively match the retained Llama, Mistral, Qwen2, Phi3 and Gemma2 architecture strings. This checks dispatch identifiers, not dimensions or defaults.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_30192523db9b4551854d885949ba7aa5",
              "call_743c4c9691844e50be87282d8685a031",
              "call_a47d9b88cad64279bea6d0952b164e52",
              "call_0f32cfeb0b554e1d89a2e80c0f9b71d1",
              "call_60cc52624f5040e1a4ecabf0888fbd0a",
              "call_3ba7866e756041489a361480d6fa41ed"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Each inspected CohereLabs config\u2014aya-23-35B, aya-23-8B, aya-expanse-32b, aya-expanse-8b, c4ai-command-r-08-2024, c4ai-command-r-plus, c4ai-command-r-plus-08-2024, c4ai-command-r-plus-4bit, c4ai-command-r-v01 and c4ai-command-r-v01-4bit\u2014declares CohereForCausalLM and therefore matches the retained dispatch identifier. No model-specific dimensional or default compatibility is asserted.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_6753a722e5e344669ea5a22a82ce0626",
              "call_81faae4311ae46fc97e24a4e22d65d4a",
              "call_9b5b6b228bdf45eb8520d8d041987ab7",
